    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Introductions (known as inter-type declarations in AspectJ) enable an aspect to declare that advised objects implement a given interface, and to provide an implementation of that interface on behalf of those objects."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "You can make an introduction by using the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@DeclareParents"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation. This annotation is used to declare that matching types have a new parent (hence the name). For example, given an interface named "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "UsageTracked"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and an implementation of that interface named "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DefaultUsageTracked"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", the following aspect declares that all implementors of service interfaces also implement the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "UsageTracked"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " interface (for example, for statistics via JMX):"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@Aspect\npublic class UsageTracking {\n\n\t@DeclareParents(value=\"com.xyz.service.*+\", defaultImpl=DefaultUsageTracked.class)\n\tpublic static UsageTracked mixin;\n\n\t@Before(\"execution(* com.xyz..service.*.*(..)) && this(usageTracked)\")\n\tpublic void recordUsage(UsageTracked usageTracked) {\n\t\tusageTracked.incrementUseCount();\n\t}\n\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@Aspect\nclass UsageTracking {\n\n\tcompanion object {\n\t\t@DeclareParents(value = \"com.xyz.service.*+\",\n\t\t\tdefaultImpl = DefaultUsageTracked::class)\n\t\tlateinit var mixin: UsageTracked\n\t}\n\n\t@Before(\"execution(* com.xyz..service.*.*(..)) && this(usageTracked)\")\n\tfun recordUsage(usageTracked: UsageTracked) {\n\t\tusageTracked.incrementUseCount()\n\t}\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The interface to be implemented is determined by the type of the annotated field. The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "value"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attribute of the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@DeclareParents"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation is an AspectJ type pattern. Any bean of a matching type implements the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "UsageTracked"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " interface. Note that, in the before advice of the preceding example, service beans can be directly used as implementations of the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "UsageTracked"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " interface. If accessing a bean programmatically, you would write the following:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "UsageTracked usageTracked = context.getBean(\"myService\", UsageTracked.class);"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "val usageTracked = context.getBean<UsageTracked>(\"myService\")"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
